## Summary
ModelDownloadViewModel.downloadWhisper converts ModelID to String and back, defeating the type safety of the ModelID wrapper.

## Location
Record-Presentation/Sources/Presentation/ViewModels/ModelDownloadViewModel.swift

## Why It Matters
Typed IDs exist to prevent bugs (e.g., confusing a model ID with a recording ID). Converting to/from String defeats this protection. At the point of the round-trip, the type information is lost—a function could be called with any string, no compile-time check.

## Suggested Fix
Keep ModelID throughout the closure chain:

```swift
// Before (wrong)
let task = Task {
    let modelString = model.id.rawValue  // ModelID → String
    let result = await downloadWhisper(modelString)
    handle(result.modelId)  // String → ModelID expected
}

// After (correct)
let task = Task {
    let result = await downloadWhisper(model.id)  // ModelID end-to-end
    handle(result.modelId)  // ModelID stays typed
}

